{"id": "EUVD-2026-76655", "enisaUuid": "d50d6054-441a-3b7a-9538-2ae26766e5c7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: nsm: bound the device-reported response length\n\nnsm_sendrecv_msg_locked() stores the virtqueue used-ring length reported\nby the NSM device into msg->resp.len without bounding it to the response\nbuffer. A malicious or buggy backend can report a length larger than the\nresponse buffer; parse_resp_raw() then copies that many bytes out of the\nfixed buffer to user space, disclosing adjacent kernel heap (an\nout-of-bounds read). The request path already floors its length in\nfill_req_raw(); the response path lacks the symmetric check.\n\nClamp the stored length to the size of the response buffer. Well-behaved\ndevices report no more than the posted buffer size, so conforming traffic\nis unaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:57", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/339f19b9a6171289b0e797deb8bda80b9a1fcc30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29e634a18957acda11383a15ab98a91c4ae9e294", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2aa0fb9c96f894a9c179a48e7522ea6705800adf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/808e530654a5354e6df78863a5d61e4d44e67235"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89743", "GHSA-ggmc-fhxw-v94j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "140acd87-0849-3bb9-aa91-7e6f60e306fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "1717c387-8db4-3210-b96f-d214a9c4f0c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1f008d12-712a-34ec-8c96-3e65309e682a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2805aac0-28bf-3ed1-be22-12497573b86a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "3b00b28c-cf4d-33c9-af90-69684752ffaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <29e634a18957acda11383a15ab98a91c4ae9e294"}, {"id": "4f921d1d-acbb-30da-bd4e-30bf64abd13f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <339f19b9a6171289b0e797deb8bda80b9a1fcc30"}, {"id": "59383632-cf4d-31fa-97d6-da4a99853fc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <808e530654a5354e6df78863a5d61e4d44e67235"}, {"id": "6d312756-a673-3274-83d5-ad7f51fd8fd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "ca3fe5b5-de5e-360b-964a-bd8181fe4554", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <2aa0fb9c96f894a9c179a48e7522ea6705800adf"}, {"id": "dc6b96d2-460b-3f84-a0ee-5e6998c9803f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "81eed2e5-cadf-38c2-886f-fc1b6ee17cd8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}